WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
ERIC ROSENBACH: This
may sound crazy, but one

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.040
of the assignments in
this course is for you

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.100
to figure out how to put a cat on Mars.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.660
Why do we do this?

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.120
Because it's a great
hypothetical example

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.060
that makes you think about the
strategy for a complex project

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.480
and then plan through
all of the processes

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.960
you need to have in place for
successful strategy execution.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.700
I'm Eric Rosenbach, Harvard Professor
and former Pentagon Chief of Staff

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.540
and Assistant Secretary of Defense for
Homeland Defense and Global Security.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.380
During my time working as Chief of
Staff at the largest organization

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.240
in the world, I worked on and witnessed
very complex issues of strategy

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.700
execution on a near-daily basis.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.440
Now, I want to try and help others
improve their ability to have impact.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:50.760
In this course, I will lead you through
real life public sector challenges

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.320
to illustrate how purposely
developed public strategies lead

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.540
to long term adoption and success.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.640
One of the great things
about this course

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.460
is that you're going to learn
directly from individuals

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:06.420
who have worked on executing complex
strategies in the real world.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:11.220
For example, Juliette Kayyem worked
as the Assistant Secretary of Homeland

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:11.520
Security.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.380
Oni Blair is currently the
Executive Director of ACLU Texas.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.160
And you'll even hear from Ash Carter,
the former Secretary of Defense.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.220
When I teach this class
here at the Kennedy School,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.480
my students are really excited to
learn about how you get things done.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:31.560
It's very rare that there's a
course on strategy execution,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.240
and that's what it's all about.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.180
They want to have impact in the
world and make a difference,

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.600
and this class helps them
learn the tools to do that.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.540
[MUSIC PLAYING]

